# Mobile-first responsive UI — agent reference

**Always-on gate:** `.cursor/rules/mobile-native-ui.mdc` (every session). This file is the full spec when editing `ui/src/**`.

Every UI component must work correctly at **375 px** (iPhone SE), **390 px** (iPhone 15), **768 px** (iPad), **1024 px** (laptop), and **1440 px** (desktop). Design mobile first; use Tailwind breakpoints to scale up, not down.

## 1. Breakpoint strategy

Use **Tailwind's default min-width breakpoints** in this order:

| Prefix   | Min width | Context                            |
| -------- | --------- | ---------------------------------- |
| _(none)_ | 0 px      | Mobile default — design here first |
| `sm:`    | 640 px    | Large phone / small tablet         |
| `md:`    | 768 px    | Tablet portrait                    |
| `lg:`    | 1024 px   | Laptop — sidebar becomes visible   |
| `xl:`    | 1280 px   | Desktop                            |

**Rules:**

- Write the mobile style first (no prefix), then add `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` overrides.
- Never write desktop-only styles without a mobile fallback.
- Never use `max-w-` breakpoints (max-width queries); always min-width.

## 2. Layout — admin dashboard

The admin shell (`AdminLayout`) follows this pattern:

```
Mobile (<lg):
  ┌────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Topbar (tenant switcher)           │
  ├────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Page content (scrolls)             │
  │  p-3 sm:p-4 + bottom tab inset     │
  ├────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ BottomTabBar (primary + More)      │
  │  or ContextualActionBar (edit)     │
  └────────────────────────────────────┘

Desktop (lg+):
  ┌──────────┬─────────────────────────┐
  │ Sidebar  │ Page content            │
  │ (flex,   │  p-5 lg:p-6             │
  │  collapsible) │                    │
  └──────────┴─────────────────────────┘
```

- Desktop sidebar is `hidden lg:flex` (collapsible width); main column fills the rest.
- On mobile, **bottom tabs** are the primary navigation: **Dashboard**, **Bookings**, **Inbox** (when present), **Notifications**, **Assistant** (when enabled), and **More**. Assistant and Notifications open the same slide-over / sheet as desktop — they are not extra header icons. Remaining pages (including Finance) live in the More sheet. The hamburger drawer is retired. More sheet nav rows use dense chrome (`text-[13px]` / `size-4` icons, 44px min height) — same scale as ModeSwitcher / list toolbars, not `text-sm` body.
- Screens with a dominant primary action (e.g. booking edit Save/Cancel) mount `ContextualActionBar`, which hides the tab bar for that route.
- Shared primitives: `ui/src/components/mobile/` (`BottomTabBar`, `BottomBarSlot`, `ContextualActionBar`, `MobileAppShell`, `PageTransition`, `MobileHeroActionMenu`, `AdminListRefineSheet`).
- **Hero trailing:** never render multiple icon buttons. Use `MobileHeroActionMenu` (1 item = direct icon; 2+ = one ··· dropdown).
- **Hero action size:** `MobileHeroActionButton` / `mobileHeroActionClassName` = visual `size-9` (36px) + invisible hit pad to ≥44px; icons `size-4`. Sticky chrome densifies further to `size-8`. Do not use `size-11` / `size-5` icons on the teal hero.
- **List toolbars (`max-lg`):** search + refine icon (`AdminListRefineSheet` for filters/sort/per-page) + view toggle — do not stack Status/Filters/Sort/Per-page as full-width rows. Desktop (`lg+`) keeps inline toolbars.
- **Dashboard density (`max-lg`):** hide page/hero subtitles (`AdminMobilePage` / `AdminPageHeader` / `MobileBrandHero` — never re-show them as body copy below `lg`), KPI decorative icons, repeated “vs last period” labels, chart icon wells/descriptions, and period eyebrows when the date filter already conveys the range. Prefer title-only section headers. **Card-header segments** (`AdminSurfaceCardHeader` actions: Name/Price, All/Income/Expenses, revenue/bookings): always **right of the title on one row**, `SegmentedControl` `size="dense"` + `equalSegments`, shared `cardHeaderSegmented*ClassName` (~28px track, 11px labels) — never stack under the title or use content-sized uneven pills. Form/toolbar segments use dense (~32px); page/section strips use compact/primary (~36px). Never `min-h-[44px]` on segment triggers (`fullWidth` for equal Sign/Upload-style pairs). Keep comfortable card/section gaps (≈10–14px gutters, `p-3`+ padding) — dense chrome, not cramped type.
- **Choice pickers (`max-lg`):** do not use tiny floating `DropdownMenu` / absolute popovers for option lists — use `MobileChoiceSheet` (≥48px rows). Applies to date presets, Guest pages, hero ··· menus, `AdminSortMenu`, `AdminSingleSelectFilter`, and similar. Desktop (`lg+`) keeps anchored menus.
- **Floating pill tab bar** — solid brand active pill; ~18px icons (stroke 1.75), 10px labels, 48px row; shared `mobileFloatingDockClassName`; tab clearance `bottomTabBarOffsetClassName()` on `MobileAppShell` for document-scroll pages, or on the **inner scrollport** for fill-main (shell `pb` there creates a dead gap and clips content). Do not use shell `p-*` shorthand or twMerge drops the clearance.
- **Sticky chrome (`max-lg`):** brand hero has a **straight bottom edge** (no arc) — scroll parallax compresses the title + bottom pad only (`--hero-collapse`), never re-adds a curve; floating toolbar (e.g. date range) straddles that seam and morphs to fixed `MobileStickyChrome` when it reaches the top (`useMobileStickyChrome`). Heavy lists: compact sticky row + More sheet. No nested scrollports. Desktop `lg+` unchanged.
- **Hero bottom pad (`max-lg`):** the tall `2.5rem` hero bottom pad only exists to seat a straddling float. Pages **without** an `overlap`/float (Inbox, Notifications, Plans, Settings, Team…) pass `MobileBrandHero flush` (`AdminMobilePage` sets it from `!overlap`) → `.mobile-brand-hero--flush` tightens it to `~0.9rem` so the title sits just above the white canvas, not over an empty green band. No `-mt-6` canvas tuck; no-float stack pad is `pt-3`.
- **Brand hero on a bespoke page:** a page that can't use `AdminMobilePage` (own workflow-first layout / own desktop header — e.g. property `BookingDetailPage`) can still render `<MobileBrandHero className="md:hidden" flush collapseProgress={useMobileHeroCollapseProgress(heroRef, isBelowMd)} />` directly. Mark its content root `data-page-brand-hero` — a scoped `@media (max-width:767px)` rule in `index.css` then drops the `AdminLayout` fallback topbar + shell gutter below `md` (tablet/desktop keep the plain topbar). Re-add the phone gutter with `max-md:px-3.5 max-md:pt-3`. The hero owns the page `h1`, so demote any in-body page heading to `h2`.
- Content language: `surface-card` floats on mobile (`shadow-native`, borderless); use `native-cta`, `native-page-canvas`, `native-stagger`, `native-press` for mockup-aligned density.
- Modals: **never render a centered desktop-style `Dialog` on mobile — anywhere (dashboard or guest).** Every modal uses `ResponsiveModal` (`ui/src/components/ui/responsive-modal.tsx`): centered `Dialog` on `lg+`, bottom sheet below `lg`. Guest-facing modals go through `GuestDialogShell` (which wraps `ResponsiveModal`). **General dashboard Save/Cancel form modals** use `AdminDialogShell` (`ui/src/components/AdminDialogShell.tsx`) — fixed title, scrollable body, fixed actions. Do not wrap custom wizards, approval reviews, lightboxes, or `AlertDialog` confirms in it. Do not import `@/components/ui/dialog` directly in feature code (only `responsive-modal` / `GuestDialogShell` / `AdminDialogShell` re-expose it). Sticky header/footer + body scroll → `sheetLayout="split"` (never `overflow-hidden` alone without a `min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto` body). Sheets size with `h-[min(92dvh,max-content)]` so tall content scrolls instead of clipping. Exceptions: `AlertDialog` for OS-style destructive confirms, and full-screen media/document lightboxes (`modal-scrim-lightbox`) that already fill the viewport.

## 2b. Layout — guest-facing marketing, booking flow, and account

Mirrors the admin shell's bottom-nav/`ContextualActionBar` pattern (§2), adapted per guest surface. All guest bottom bars share the same `ui/src/components/mobile/` primitives (`BottomBarSlotProvider`, `BottomTabBar`, `ContextualActionBar`, `bottomTabBarOffsetClassName`) — never a bespoke hand-rolled `fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0` bar.

- **Marketing site** (`MarketingLayoutShell`, everything under `/`, `/properties`, `/parkings`, `/developments`, `/for-hosts*`, `/account/*`, legal/about/contact/support): `MarketingLayoutShell` wraps its `Outlet` in `BottomBarSlotProvider`; `MarketingBottomNav.tsx` renders a 5-tab `BottomTabBar` (Explore, Properties, Parkings — active-matches `/developments` too, Account, More) that is mode-aware (guest/Explore vs host/`for-hosts` mode swaps the Account tab's resolved href and the More sheet's sign-in link via `getAuthAudienceFromPath`/`getAppModeFromPath`). `MarketingMoreSheet.tsx` holds secondary links (For hosts/Company/Legal groups from the same source as `MarketingFooter`), `ThemeToggle`, the reused `ModeSwitcher`, **Dashboard** when signed in, and sign out. `MarketingNav.tsx`'s top header stays fixed but is logo-only on phone (nav links/CTA/account are `lg:flex`-gated) — the hamburger + full-screen `AnimatePresence` overlay it used to render on `<lg` is retired entirely; do not resurrect it.
- **Guest account section** (`/account/*`, nested inside the marketing shell above): keeps its **own top** `GuestAccountMobileNav` strip (`sticky top-16 z-30 lg:hidden`, `SlidingActivePill`) for Profile/Stays/Vouchers/Favorites/Tickets — **do not** turn this into a second bottom `BottomTabBar`. `/account/*` already renders the marketing-wide bottom tab bar above; a second bottom bar for the account sub-section would stack two bottom navs on one screen (`avoid-mixed-patterns` / `bottom-nav-top-level`). This mirrors how admin's Settings sub-nav stays top-level chrome rather than becoming a second dock.
- **Property/parking operational flow** (`MainLayout`, `/properties/:slug/{calendar,messages,form,success,sd-form,guest-review,parking/:id}`): `MainLayout` takes optional `bottomTabs`/`bottomTabsActiveKey` props — when passed (property routes only), it wraps in the same `BottomBarSlotProvider` + `BottomTabBar` (Property/Calendar/Messages, 3 items). A wizard step with one dominant Back/Continue/Submit action (`GuestFormStepNavigation`'s `mobileVariant="floating"`, or a page's own `useIsBelowLg()` + `ContextualActionBar` wrap) auto-hides the tab bar for that route via the shared slot — exactly the admin edit-form pattern. Screens with no single dominant action (`guest-review`, `sd-form` steps 1–2, the legacy `parking/:bookingId` redirect stub) correctly keep the tab bar visible; don't force a `ContextualActionBar` onto them. Single-purpose pages reached outside this shell (`PayParkingPage` standalone route, `ParkingRequestStatusPage`, `ParkingFormPage`) omit `bottomTabs` entirely — no tab bar, no siblings to switch between. A component whose nav renders in more than one context (`GuestFormStepNavigation` in the modal `GuestBookingFormModal` vs. the standalone `/form` route; `ParkingRegistrationForm` in `ParkingBookingFormModal` vs. `ParkingFormPage`) takes an explicit `mobileVariant`/similar prop so the modal-embedded render stays a plain inline row — a page-level fixed `ContextualActionBar` would fight the modal's own sheet chrome.
- **Auth pages** (`AuthLayout`, `/for-hosts/login`, `/for-hosts/register`, `/for-guests/login`, `/for-guests/register`): registered as their own top-level route array, never nested inside `MarketingLayoutShell` — **no bottom tab bar by default** (linear trust-flow convention). Keep the existing mobile top bar (logo + `ThemeToggle`, `lg:hidden`) rather than adding one.

## 3. Touch targets

All interactive elements must meet **WCAG 2.5.5 (AAA) / iOS HIG**: minimum **44 × 44 px**.

```tsx
// ✅ Good — icon button with explicit min size
<button className="p-2.5 rounded-lg min-w-[44px] min-h-[44px] flex items-center justify-center">

// ❌ Bad — icon button too small
<button className="p-1 rounded">
```

Table row actions, filter buttons, nav items, and pagination chips must all meet this threshold. Use `py-2.5` or `min-h-[44px]` on any tappable element.

## 4. Typography scaling

Native-app density on phone (≈ iOS HIG ops apps). Prefer shared tokens in `ui/src/index.css`.

| Use                         | Mobile                                                                                                                                                                   | Desktop                         |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| Hero / page title           | `text-lg` (`text-admin-page-title`, hero h1)                                                                                                                             | `sm:text-xl` → `md:text-2xl`    |
| Section title               | `text-sm` (`text-section-title`)                                                                                                                                         | `sm:text-[15px]`                |
| Card title                  | `text-sm` (`text-card-title`)                                                                                                                                            | `sm:text-base`                  |
| Card description            | `text-xs` (`text-card-description`)                                                                                                                                      | `sm:text-sm`                    |
| Body / UI                   | `text-sm` (`text-ui`)                                                                                                                                                    | same                            |
| KPI / stat value            | `text-base` (`text-stat-value`)                                                                                                                                          | `sm:text-xl` → `md:text-2xl`    |
| List amount                 | `text-[15px]` (`text-list-amount`)                                                                                                                                       | `sm:text-base`                  |
| Secondary / muted           | `text-xs` (`text-data-secondary`, `text-meta`)                                                                                                                           | `sm:text-[13px]` / `sm:text-sm` |
| Overflow (⋯) menus          | `admin-overflow-trigger` (32px visual + expanded hit) — never outline `min-h-[44px]` boxes on phone                                                                      | same or labeled Manage          |
| Settings secondary CTA      | `settings-action` — visual `h-8` + text-xs; ≥44px via invisible pad (**never** `min-h-[44px]` on the box) — Manage / Customize / Test / Archive                          | same                            |
| Settings field label        | `settings-field-label` (12px muted)                                                                                                                                      | `sm:text-sm` foreground         |
| Tabs / segments (dashboard) | `text-[13px]` (form/toolbar = `SegmentedControl` dense (~h-8); section strips = compact/primary (~h-9); never `h-9`/`p-1` or `min-h-[44px]` overrides on dense triggers) | same                            |
| List search fields          | `text-[13px]` placeholder/value on phone                                                                                                                                 | `lg:text-sm`                    |
| Table data                  | `text-sm`                                                                                                                                                                | `text-[13px]`                   |
| Caption / overline          | `text-[10px]`–`text-xs`                                                                                                                                                  | same                            |

**Do not** bump phone titles with `max-sm:text-[1.65rem]` or KPI values with `text-lg`/`text-2xl` on `max-lg` — that reads oversized vs native apps.

**Marketing display exception:** full-bleed marketing heroes (`MarketingPublicPageHero`, for-hosts film, stay-guide showcase templates) may use `text-3xl`–`text-5xl`. Do **not** apply that display scale to admin chrome, guest form/account/auth, listing cards, or operational public flows.

## 5. Tables

Tables must never cause horizontal overflow on the page. Use this pattern:

```tsx
<div className="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl">
  {' '}
  {/* scrollable wrapper */}
  <table className="w-full min-w-[600px]">
    {' '}
    {/* ensures table doesn't collapse */}
    ...
  </table>
</div>
```

Hide non-critical columns on small screens:

| Column                    | Visible from                 |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Status                    | always                       |
| Guest (name + email)      | always                       |
| Stay (dates + nights)     | always                       |
| Pax                       | `md:`                        |
| Flags (parking/pet icons) | `sm:`                        |
| Amount                    | `lg:`                        |
| Created                   | `md:`                        |
| Actions                   | always (icon only on mobile) |

## 6. Forms and filter bars

- Search input: always full-width (`w-full`).
- Filter button strips: `overflow-x-auto` horizontal scroll on mobile — never wrap into multiple rows.
- Dropdown panels: on `max-lg`, prefer `MobileChoiceSheet` / `ResponsiveOverflowMenu` over floating `DropdownMenu` panels. Desktop keeps `DropdownMenu`. Position absolute panels on desktop: `max-h-[60vh] overflow-y-auto`, with a max-width of `min(90vw, 320px)` to avoid viewport overflow.
- Input height: `h-10` (40 px) minimum — touch friendly. `Input`, `Select` (`SelectTrigger`), and `Textarea` primitives all self-align to `h-10` / `px-3` **on mobile** (`max-lg:`) so a form column of mixed controls lines up; desktop keeps the wider `Select` `h-11` / `px-4`. Don't re-add per-call-site `h-10` overrides just to compensate.
- Modal / sheet titles: `ResponsiveModalTitle` renders the same scale in sheet mode (phone/tablet) as `DialogTitle` on desktop — `text-base font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-lg`. Don't hard-code `text-lg` as the mobile base on a modal title.

## 7. Spacing

| Context            | Mobile       | Desktop        |
| ------------------ | ------------ | -------------- |
| Page padding       | `p-3 sm:p-4` | `lg:p-6`       |
| Card / section gap | `space-y-3`  | `sm:space-y-4` |
| Form field gap     | `space-y-4`  | same           |
| Inline button gap  | `gap-1.5`    | same           |

Never use `px-6` or larger without a mobile fallback like `px-4`.

## 8. Images and media

- Always set explicit `width` + `height` or use `aspect-*` classes.
- Use `object-cover` on images inside fixed containers.
- Never use `<img>` inside a flex container without `shrink-0` or `min-w-0`.

## 9. Modals and dropdowns

- **No centered modal on mobile (app-wide):** every modal — confirms, forms, pickers, detail panels, guest booking/calendar modals — uses `ResponsiveModal` (centered `Dialog` on `lg+`, bottom sheet below `lg`); guest modals via `GuestDialogShell`; general dashboard form modals via `AdminDialogShell`. Never import `@/components/ui/dialog` directly in feature code. Sticky chrome → `sheetLayout="split"` + `min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto` body. Only `AlertDialog` (OS-style destructive confirm) and full-screen media/document lightboxes stay non-sheet. Avoid full-screen `fixed inset-0` sheets unless intentionally a full-page flow.
- Dropdowns / overflow menus: on `max-lg`, use `MobileChoiceSheet` or `ResponsiveOverflowMenu` (`ui/src/components/mobile/ResponsiveOverflowMenu.tsx`) instead of floating `DropdownMenu` panels. Marketing menus can use `MarketingOverflowMenu`. Desktop keeps `DropdownMenu`. If a legacy dropdown remains on mobile, apply `max-w-[calc(100vw-24px)]` as a safety net.
- Use `z-50` for overlays, `z-40` for sticky headers and the bottom tab / contextual bar.

## 10. Don'ts

- Don't hardcode pixel widths that assume desktop: `width: 800px` without `max-w-full`.
- Don't use `whitespace-nowrap` on text that should wrap at mobile sizes.
- Don't hide entire feature sections behind `hidden lg:block` without providing a mobile alternative.
- Don't make the sidebar navigation invisible on mobile without a topbar replacement.
- Don't use `overflow-hidden` on the `<body>` or root layout — it breaks iOS momentum scrolling.
- Don't add `hover:` effects without checking they degrade gracefully on touch (no hover state).
- Don't use fixed `height` on containers that hold dynamic text content.

## 11. Testing checklist (before shipping any UI change)

- [ ] Works at 375 px width (Chrome DevTools, iPhone SE profile)
- [ ] Works at 768 px width (iPad portrait)
- [ ] No horizontal scroll at any breakpoint (unless intentional + inside a scrollable container)
- [ ] All tap targets ≥ 44 × 44 px
- [ ] Text is readable without zooming at 375 px
- [ ] Table does not overflow viewport
- [ ] Dropdown panels do not overflow viewport
- [ ] Filter bar is usable on mobile (scrollable strip or dropdown)
